// This anchor is the shape of a design that a project imports from an Emul
// file. The module hook of the Emul plugin makes one concrete emul-design
// anchor for each design that the Emul file exports. This file is part of the bundled Emul plugin, as
// @piton/emul.
export abstract anchor EmulDesign as emul-design:
    name:: string
    kind:: string
    file:: string

    usage:
        `${self.name}` is an Emul ${self.kind} in `${self.file}`. The path is
        relative to the project root. The `emul` compiler is already installed
        on this system. Do not install it. To use the design, read the Emul
        file directly, or compile the design to SVG, PNG or HTML with `emul
        build`. Select the form that is most useful for the current work. SVG
        and PNG show how the design looks. HTML shows the structure and the
        CSS. The Emul source shows the exact values. Write compiled files to a
        temporary directory with `--out`, and do not add them to the project.
        `emul build` renders only compositions that the entry of an Emul
        project exports. Thus give `--config` for the Emul project of the
        file, or make a temporary Emul project whose entry exports the design.
        A component shows only in a composition.
